 {"id": "QA-AUGER-14", "title": "[P2] live-arm suite must fail fast (named cause) when a full-fleet sync push or a sibling pytest leg holds the substrate — instead of burning 61s x N in backoff and reporting 106 phantom errors", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-10-23T07:00:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-25T04:50:38Z", "created_by": "auger-foreman", "capability_tags": ["tests", "conftest", "reproducibility"], "reasoning": "QA-AUGER-13 measured the real cause of the 1802s / 106-error audit run: conftest teardown TEARDOWN_CONFLICT_BACKOFFS=(1,2,4,8,16,30)=61s is exhausted whenever a full-fleet `duckbrain.js s3 sync all push` (deadline 3600s) holds a namespace native sync lock, and 992s of the 992.88s delta over the 810s baseline is that ladder x ~16 live namespaces. A missing DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY only produces SKIPS, never errors. Second, a foreign pytest leg holding /tmp/auger-pytest-substrate.lock serializes whole sessions, so a second full run waits with no visible reason. Both make a 30-minute red ambiguous: the operator cannot tell an environment collision from a code defect without reading teardown internals. CORRECTION (verdict-driven, 07:10Z): the second lock holder was NOT a foreign lane. pid 2781984 was the ORPHANED pytest child of this tick's own dispatched worker (launcher pid 2781981, started 01:44:16 local, cmd `pytest tests/ -q -ra`, log /tmp/qa13_run.log); when the worker session died its launcher scope went away and the run was reparented to systemd --user, so it kept holding /tmp/auger-pytest-substrate.lock while writing into /tmp/qa13_run.log (at 41% and 19m39s elapsed when found). Attribution corrected here; the finding itself stands and is worse than \"foreign lane\": a killed worker leaves a flock-holding orphan that silently blocks every later run, and no preflight names it. SECOND FINDING: a single 409 collision leaks its test namespace, and the later leak-audit test then fails on that residue (the orphan log shows EFF at 20% inside the 01:30:30-01:51 sync-push window, then an isolated F at 41% after the push had ended). One lock collision therefore cascades into fixes-later-in-the-run reds, which is exactly the ambiguity QA-AUGER-14 must remove. The orphan has been reaped (SIGTERM to the process group); the lock file is free. Preflight must therefore also detect an orphaned flock holder, not only a running sync push, and must clear leaked test namespaces before the leak audit runs.", "acceptance_criteria": "1) tests/conftest.py gains a session-start preflight that detects (a) a full-fleet sync push (pgrep -af \"duckbrain.js s3 sync all push\" or a probe DELETE answering 409 \"Push in flight\") and (b) a foreign holder of AUGER_TEST_LOCK, and fails fast with a single named line naming the pid and the cause (e.g. \"AUGER_BLOCKED_BY: full-fleet sync push pid N\") when AUGER_REQUIRE_LIVE=1, or marks live arms skipped-with-reason otherwise. 2) A regression test proves the preflight fires on a simulated 409 and does not fire when the locks are free. 3) The 61s ladder stays for the ordinary post-write window (unchanged behaviour when no push is in flight). 4) A fresh clean-venv full run with the locks free is captured green (0 failed, 0 errors) within the 2400s budget, closing QA-AUGER-13 criterion 3.\n\nMIGRATED from the legacy acceptance field (PM union 2026-10-24):\nPASS: `grep -c 'AUGER_BLOCKED_BY' tests/conftest.py` prints at least 2 (one named-cause line per detector: full-fleet sync push, foreign substrate-lock holder), `grep -c 'duckbrain.js s3 sync all push' tests/conftest.py` prints at least 1, and `grep -c 'LOCK_NB' tests/conftest.py` prints at least 1 — push detection plus a NON-BLOCKING lock probe; all three print 0 today, so this clause cannot pass on the pre-fix tree. PASS: `grep -n -A60 'def live_service' tests/conftest.py | grep -c 'AUGER_BLOCKED_BY'` prints at least 1 — the emitter is reachable from the session-scoped fixture that takes the substrate lock,