 {"id": "GATE-RED-001", "title": "[P1] main's live-arm gate is RED: test_the_default_decision_scope_is_project_and_sends_no_scope_key fails because the stored D-001 row carries scope='project'", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-10-23T13:55:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-23T15:40:00Z", "created_by": "auger-foreman-2026-10-23-13-10-25", "capability_tags": ["tests", "scope", "substrate-drift", "gate"], "reasoning": "Wave-recovery tick auger-foreman-2026-10-23-13-10-25 re-ran `bash tests/gate.sh` on main (HEAD a7ee546, == origin/main) as required by the recovery manifest for auger-foreman-2026-10-23-04-34-27. The gate is RED at the pytest arm: `python3 -m pytest tests/test_auger.py tests/test_openapi_parity.py tests/test_api_service.py -q -x --tb=short` stops at tests/test_auger.py:1331 test_the_default_decision_scope_is_project_and_sends_no_scope_key with `AssertionError: a decision written without --scope carries one: {'id': 'D-001', ..., 'scope': 'project'}` (1 failed, 45 passed in 166.89s, log /tmp/auger-recovery-firstfail.log). AUG-009's contract is that a default-scope decision OMITS the scope key (auger.py decision_scope/insert_decision, UNDECLARED_SCOPE fallback near auger.py:4789-4845); the test asserts the API row has no scope key while the later disk assertion tolerates the declared column materialised as null. So either (a) auger now sends scope for the default path — a contract regression against AUG-009, or (b) the substrate/declared-table layer now materialises a default for the declared column and returns it on read — a substrate drift that the test's read-back premise cannot survive. Which side drifted must be proven from bytes, not guessed. This red is invisible to hosted CI because ci.yml sets AUGER_CI=1 and skips the live arms, so main can show green CI while the local full gate is red; it blocks every later tick's gate and QA-AUGER-13/QA-AUGER-14 criterion 4.", "acceptance_criteria": "1) The failing assertio