irectory and asserts it appears in neither stream nor in the refusal detail.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-13T13:51:40.644396+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-14T13:54:41.333933+00:00", "foreman_note": "Dispatched 2026-11-14 driver tick from origin/main ee6e7bf into /home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-169 (wt/AUG-169). Verified at base: _spec_discover_documents iterates root.rglob(\"*.xml\"), which does NOT descend symlinked directories, so an out-of-root symlinked directory is neither read, refused nor counted; shipped pins -k symlink = 2 passed; gate pytest arm names tests/test_xml_specs.py at tests/gate.sh:206. Existing file-level rule (symlink-outside-root at auger.py:8023) and dangling-link rule (unreadable-document) are the precedents to extend. Worker must keep the A2 sweep agreeing and add the new pin in tests/test_xml_specs.py.\n\nClosed on judged PASS afc16739 (.gitreins/history/2026-11-14/afc16739/verdict.json; task_id=AUG-169, commit=09ed733, pass_class=judged). tier1 lint/secrets/tests PASS = bash tests/gate.sh GATE PASS, 729 passed / 2 skipped in 840.16s, LIVE ARMS ran 2 / skipped 0. tier2 9/9 items PASS (5 authored + 4 derived), 0 ungraded, merge_recommendation=no_concerns_found. Implementation 6b806ac merged to main, lifecycle 09ed733 graded; exact-head CI run 43597431860 success. Driver re-measured all four row ACs independently first: 1 passed / 3 passed / grep 2 / out-of-root directory link refused rc 2 symlink-outside-root by BOTH verbs with sentinel count 0 in both streams; A2 sweep 7/7 AGREE. Residual observation (not a defect): an IN-root directory symlink duplicating an already-walked file yields a typed duplicate-id refusal rather than dedupe.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "6b806accea435caad6350fdf46278b591248eba4", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-169", "branch": "wt/AUG-169", "evidence_run_id": "afc16739"}
