atus, with the reason recorded in its note. FAILIF: any id still complete AND citing passed=false.\nAC3 PROOF: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py -q` prints all passed, including a NEW test that hands the audit a synthetic complete row citing a passed=false verdict and asserts the row is named as a defect; that new test fails against scripts/audit_board_evidence.py at 1b54668 (red-proof pasted into evidence/AUG-182/). FAILIF: the new test passes unchanged against the pre-fix script, or no new test exists.\nAC4 PROOF: `bash tests/gate.sh` ends GATE PASS with the new test file named in the pytest arm of tests/gate.sh. FAILIF: GATE FAIL, or the test is not in the arm.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-17T12:53:38Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-17T12:53:38Z", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": null}
