ration is therefore path-of-invocation dependent and will silently re-point a committed manifest when run from a worktree. Row stays in_progress because no GitReins verdict exists for aab0e5e, so no evidence_run_id is claimed (verdict debt).", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "aab0e5ea6b04ae70e637d61d3df4353c20c70331", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": null, "worker_summary": "CI-red fix certified by judged verdict 6db67ef6: tier1 GATE PASS 797 passed / 2 skipped in 872.82s, live arms 2/0; tier2 PASS 5/5 with the evaluator re-running every proof.", "evidence_run_id": "6db67ef6"}
+-{"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-184", "title": "[P2] acceptance-criteria repair: 14 of 27 open rows fail the deterministic dispatchability gate on unexpanded placeholders, so workers must invent paths and commands", "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "8eaafc9c1c7716fe4794c74fb38ed978ead003aaf8abfec4b0b9234f32c8679e"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "COS card manager measurement 2026-11-17T14:35Z on board @700ec56: `python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/acceptance_gate.py audit /home/kara/auger` reports 27 open rows, 14 failing, 13 passing. Every failure is the placeholder arm (angle-bracket stubs such as a bare token, namespace, key, run id, corpus path, verb name) with a few also failing the path arm where a criteria line names a path that is not in this repo's git ls-files (AUG-178's src/search/index.ts is duckbrain-owned) and one failing the outcome arm. The consequence is measurable: the open rows on this board are not re-runnable by a worker with no context, so each dispatch re-derives paths and commands from scratch, and the gate cannot be used as a dispatch filter. This is mechanical criteria maintenance — paths, commands and observables already exist in each row's own reasoning — not a redesign of any requirement, which is why it is filed as one chore rather than 14 edits by an out-of-lane writer. The COS does not rewrite foreman rows mid-flight (guardrail 2). Goal cards citing this work: t_a2ee1356 (QA trust) for the QA-plane rows, t_d7ac1156 (docs parity) for the DOC/doc-plane rows, t_35d10e68 (corpus/search) for the corpus rows.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "AC1 CENSUS ZERO: Run `python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/acceptance_gate.py audit /home/kara/auger | grep -c '^FAIL'`; expect the printed count to be 0 (measured 2026-11-17: 14). FAILIF: any FAIL line remains.\nAC2 SAME INTENT, RUNNABLE ARMS: Run `python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/acceptance_gate.py audit /home/kara/auger`; expect a PASS line for each of AUG-152, AUG-153, AU