+ {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-148", "title": "Symlinked spec files are followed out of the corpus root, while <include src> outside the root is refused", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b500c7e493f3caee48b8bc4b5b4ee649e488348aea7fd66cd956f100cd93150e", "evidence": [{"run_id": "f12e309e", "ts": "2026-11-13T15:58:19.606984+00:00"}]}, "priority": "P3", "source": null, "reasoning": "Deep pass 2026-11-05 at cf5bfe2: with linked.xml -> /etc/hostname inside the corpus, `spec validate` reads and parses the target ('spec error (invalid-xml): linked.xml: syntax error'), i.e. the loader followed a symlink outside the root and consumed host-file bytes. By contrast <include src=\"/etc/hostname\"/> is refused with remote-reference-rejected ('only repository-relative local files are allowed'). The out-of-root rule is therefore enforced on one mechanism and bypassable on the other.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a symlink whose target resolves outside the corpus root is refused with a typed error (or skipped with an explicit count), proven by a fixture that links to a file outside the root.\nPASS: a symlink whose target stays inside the root keeps working (no over-blocking), proven by the paired positive fixture.\nPASS: the rule is stated once and applied to both mechanisms — include and file discovery — and a test asserts both paths produce the same class of refusal.\nPASS: no host-file content can reach stdout/stderr beyond the typed diagnostic naming the path (asserted by grepping the error text for target content).", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:24:13.639428+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-13T15:58:19.606984+00:00", "foreman_note": "2026-11-05 wave: merged on main 6b0d190 (spec-a 7bb5565/c6b24b3/c84f617, spec-b 4b27c83/8375d78/35267f6, corpus 20731e8); full gate on merged tree GATE PASS rc=0, 485 passed/2 skipped, live arms 2/0; targeted 113 passed; verdict still outstanding (no fabricated run id)\n\n2026-11-13 driver: NOT closed — two instrument failures, both measured. (1) Judge run 52162def at 6692f62 red-ed tier1 on 2 board-evidence audit tests caused by 6692f62 closing QA-AUGER-16/REVIEW-1/RELENG-1 with no evidence_run_id; fixed in 58f5af4 (closed-vocabulary none:no-verdict-artifact-for-task-id, audit RESULT: OK, 17 tests green, CI success). (2) Judge run 4bd93bbe at 58f5af4: tier1 PASS (gate green), tier2 all 8 criteria graded, 5/5 authored PASS, then 'Iteration cap (400) reached (400.3 used)' → INCOMPLETE/passed=false; the evaluator spent 400 iterations on derived probes of the discovery path. Re-judge with GITREINS_MAX_ITERATIONS=800 / 16M next. Residual finding filed as AUG-169: a symlinked DIRECTORY resolving outside the root is silently ignored (no refusal, no count). No fabricated run id.\n\n2026-11-13 driver r4: judged PASS at 01f1904. Verdict .gitreins/history/2026-11-13/f12e309e/verdict.json task_id=AUG-148 commit=01f1904 passed=true pass_class=judged; tier1 lint/secrets/tests PASS = real bash tests/gate.sh GATE PASS 722 passed / 2 skipped in 841.76s, LIVE ARMS ran 2 skipped 0; tier2 COMPLETE 9/9 PASS (5 authored + 4 derived), ungraded_criteria none. Product commit d024c19 (fix(spec): refuse a symlink that resolves outside the corpus root) proven by -S symbol search, ancestor of main. Prior instrument reds preserved: 52162def (foreign QA board evidence) and 4bd93bbe (iteration cap 400 -> INCOMPLETE at 58f5af4); r4 honoured GITREINS_MAX_ITERATIONS=800/16M. Residual: symlinked DIRECTORY outside root silently ignored -> filed AUG-169.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "commit_hash": "d024c193b0358c8faeacf841c6c434976bb84870", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "symlink discovery refusal judged PASS (run f12e309e)", "evidence_run_id": "f12e309e"}
+ {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-149", "title": "A no-match selection returns rc 0 with empty output and no diagnostic", "detail": {"fingerprint": "853e1f9ba0a77f73768420a99a94a1378b0ee160161e3de97694e81c9d789d5a", "evidence": [{"run_id": "277112c1", "ts": "2026-11-13T16:20:47.549045+00:00"}]}, "priority": "P4", "source": null, "reasoning": "Deep pass 2026-11-05 at cf5bfe2: `auger spec list <corpus> --applies-to nope.none` exits 0 with zero bytes on stdout and nothing on stderr, and the same holds for `--version 3.0.0`. The PRD's finding taxonomy names 'no match' as a reportable selection finding, and a caller scripting the CLI cannot distinguish 'your selector matched nothing' from 'the tool had nothing to say' without parsing emptiness. The empty-selector case is already refused correctly ('empty-selector'), so the contract is inconsistent between the two shapes.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a selector that matches nothing reports it explicitly (a one-line notice on stderr or a typed empty result with a count of 0) while keeping stdout machine-parseable; asserted by a test on both `spec list` and `spec assemble`.\nPASS: the exit code contract is stated in the README/help and matches behaviour for the three shapes: no selector, selector with no match, selector with matches.\nPASS: existing consumers are not broken by the change: `--format json` still emits a valid document with an empty selection and exit code 0 unless the README says otherwise.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:24:13.725478+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-13T16:20:47.549045+00:00", "foreman_note": "2026-11-05 wave: merged on main 6b0d190 (spec-a 7bb5565/c6b24b3/c84f617, spec-b 4b27c83/8375d78/35267f6, corpus 20731e8); full gate on merged tree GATE PASS rc=0, 485 passed/2 skipped, live arms 2/0; targeted 113 passed; verdict still outstanding (no fabricated run id)\n\n2026-11-13 driver: judged PASS at bd506c3. Verdict .gitreins/history/2026-11-13/